Here are some of the things I had suggested (from a modified version of
rogue) that weren't added to hack.  (This is where the wizard & the mail
daemon originated; there are a few versions of my rogue around MN, I
understand).  The last few are new suggestions.

---

Scroll of duplication
This is a scroll of duplication--More--
This is a scroll of duplication--More--
    Allows you to duplicate an item.  Caveats with wands of wishing, etc.
    If you duplicate itself, you can "save" it, since the original
    vanishes.  Just gives you 1 more of the item, if you duplicate
    3 knives.  Cursed ought to make a cursed duplicate & destroy the
    original.  Should Blessed make a blessed copy?

Wand of clone monster
    Obvious.  Cloning a mimic produces a "hiding" mimic, in case
    the room is dark...  "Blessed" should make many clones.

Wand of everything
    This is a fun one, but a bit tricky to implement.  When zapped,
    it picks a random wand effect and does that.  The tricky part is
    "identifying" it as, say, a wand of digging on the first zap,
    and then as a wand of everything on a subsequent zap.  Easiest
    way around this is to simply identify it as whatever it was
    zapped as most recently, and let the player name it.
    Can be a real killer - first zap to call it a wand of death,
    second zap as haste...

Wand of fireballs
    I had changed the wand of fire to zap a distance, then
    explode, thus:
         \!/
    @----=*=
         /!\
    This gives damage to everything in the 3x3 area, with more
    damage to the center.  NetHack could use an area-effect weapon...
    The bolt doesn't bounce, if it hits anything it explodes.
    It also explodes after travelling the max bolt distance (which
    varies a bit).  Should "dig" a one-square hole if it hits a wall.
    Maybe this should just be a blessed wand of fire.

Wand of lightning
    I had changed this to be accurate at 2 squares, chancier at
    farther distances, by doing:
        ---
    @---   --
	     ---
    In words, the "bolt", like lightning, zigzags.  Makes for
    interesting bounces, too!  Could be just a cursed lightning
    wand acts this way.

Ring of wand charges
    Ring with a few zaps in it.  When you zap an empty wand, the
    ring glows and gives the wand a free zap.  Shouldn't work for
    wishing, of course.

Ring of weakness
    Works like regeneration, but removes 1 HP each turn, if your
    hit points are more than half your maximum.  Two of these
    should allow you to drain to 0...

When you fall in water, your scrolls should all turn blank and
your potions should all be water, a la' cancellation.
Books should turn blank, too.  Does it do this now?
I don't have hack right here to test...

A book "+" might be a volume of "Magic Potions A-L" instead of plaid, etc.
Reading it will identify potions starting with A-L, i.e. you now know
what color a "healing" potion is, a "blindness" potion, but it won't
tell you the color of "paralysis", etc.  Two volumes each for
potions, scroll, rings, wands.  Make them rare...

I would sometimes put guardian monsters inside chests (appropriate
ones only) that come out aggravated.  floating eyes, bats, rats,
snakes, gremins, etc. would all be good.

Chests should occasionally contain all of the same type of object
(all potions, all scrolls, etc).  A good gag that I pulled was
a chest of chests would only contain chests of chests, that is,
you open up the chest and only find more chests, which only contain
more chests, etc, etc.  Polymorph would probably be too powerful
on an infinite chest of chests, so polymorph shouldn't affect it.
(you could generate a huge number of chests & then polymorph them
into useful items).  Maybe have ONE item in them, somewhere.
It would be easy to keep a value around, which says "there is an
item 5 chests in", and when it is opened and 3 chests are found,
it is changed to 4 and assigned to ONE of the chests.  Keep going
until you find the one chest with the good item (like a wand of
wishing).  With an average of only 3 chests in each chest, 5 chests
in, there are 3^5=243 chests at that level, and you'd have to open
about half of them to find it.  Identify scroll might help...
Risks an out of memory panic, too.  heh, heh.

If you put a bag of holding in itself, it should disappear, taking
all objects inside with it.

Blessed scroll of amnesia should make you forget what all the types
of magic are (i.e. you forget that a blue potion is healing, or whatever).
You, of course, forget what scroll is amnesia, too.

Blessed ring of teleport control should allow you to zap a monster
with teleportation and control where it lands.

"What direction?" should also accept control chars of hjklyubn,
as I am always doing ^D^L instead of ^DL.  Unless ^H=backspace
is a problem...

